{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"thermal-queasy-watussi","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nThe rebar 0.11.0 post-release check proved that `gh attestation verify <wheel> --repo navapbc/rebar` cannot verify the PEP 740 bundle produced by pypa/gh-action-pypi-publish. The command queries GitHub Artifact Attestations for SLSA provenance; the publish action uploads a `https://docs.pypi.org/attestations/publish/v1` bundle to PyPI. The official `pypi-attestations verify pypi` command validates the published wheel successfully.\n\n## Plan\n- Add a regression oracle for the documented provenance-verification command/semantics.\n- Replace the incorrect GitHub-store verifier in docs/releasing.md with the authoritative PyPI PEP 740 verifier and correct the matching release-workflow comment.\n- Preserve the separate GitHub immutable-release attestation semantics without conflating them with PyPI provenance.\n- Run focused documentation/workflow tests and the relevant gates.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The runbook verifies a downloaded PyPI artifact with the official PyPI attestation verifier and repository identity.\n- [ ] The runbook no longer claims that a GitHub SLSA lookup proves the PyPI PEP 740 bundle.\n- [ ] The release workflow comment names the correct consumer verifier and store.\n- [ ] A regression test protects the documented command and predicate/store distinction.\n- [ ] Focused tests, lint, and typecheck pass.","id":"13b4-c597-200b-4e31","parent_id":"","priority":2,"tags":["release","docs","supply-chain"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"PyPI provenance runbook uses GitHub-only attestation verifier"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786085650260876001,"uuid":"4b53f730-ee00-48c0-b657-b8259b0eb6ec"}